// @@@ If the index is between 0 and the size of the list inclusive, then for every valid index from the insertion point to the old size of the list, the element at each subsequent index after the insertion is either null and was null before, or is equal to the element that was at the previous index before the insertion.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is between 0 and the size of the list inclusive, then for every valid index from the insertion point to the previous end of the list, the element at each subsequent position is either both null or the same as the element at the current position before insertion.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is between 0 and the size of the list inclusive, then for every valid index from the insertion point to the old size of the list, the element at the next position is either null if the old element at this index was null, or equal to the old element at this index.
